8. SYSTEM DESIGN
8.1 System Flow
•	User opens the AI Weather Wise application.
•	User enters a city or selects My Location.
•	The application obtains latitude and longitude.
•	The application sends the coordinates to the weather API.
•	The API returns weather information.
•	JavaScript processes the returned JSON data.
•	Current weather and seven-day forecast are displayed.
•	The recommendation engine analyzes weather conditions.
•	Smart advice is displayed to the user.
8.2 Architecture
The system follows a simple client-side architecture. The browser contains the user interface and application logic. The JavaScript code communicates directly with external API endpoints. The basic version does not require a custom backend database.
User → Web Interface → JavaScript → Geocoding API → Coordinates → Weather API → Weather Data → Recommendation Engine → User Interface
9. MODULE DESCRIPTION
9.1 City Search Module
This module accepts a city name from the user and sends it to the geocoding service. The first matching location is used to obtain latitude and longitude.
9.2 Weather Data Module
This module sends geographical coordinates to the weather forecast service and retrieves current and daily weather information.
9.3 Current Weather Module
This module displays temperature, weather condition, humidity, wind speed, precipitation, and cloud cover.
9.4 Forecast Module
This module processes daily forecast arrays and creates cards for seven days showing the day, weather icon, condition, maximum and minimum temperature, and precipitation.
9.5 Smart Recommendation Module
The recommendation module applies predefined rules to weather values. For example, high rainfall can result in an umbrella recommendation, high temperature can produce a hydration recommendation, and thunderstorm codes can produce a safety warning.
9.6 Location Module
The location module uses the browser Geolocation API to obtain the user's coordinates after permission is granted. These coordinates are sent to the weather service.
10. IMPLEMENTATION
The complete application is implemented in one HTML file. The file contains three logical parts: HTML markup, CSS styling inside the style section, and JavaScript inside the script section.
10.1 Main API Endpoints
Geocoding endpoint: https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search
Forecast endpoint: https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast
10.2 Important JavaScript Functions
•	getWeather() – reads the city name and searches for coordinates.
•	loadWeather() – requests forecast data using latitude and longitude.
•	displayWeather() – updates the current weather section.
•	generateAIAdvice() – generates rule-based weather recommendations.
•	displayForecast() – creates the seven-day forecast cards.
•	getLocation() – requests weather using browser location.
•	showLoading() – displays or hides the loading message.
